---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import DesignTodo from './DesignTodo.astro';
import '../styles/raices.css';
const { locale='en' }=Astro.props; const es=locale==='es'; const root=es?'/es/':'/';
const areas=[['THERAPY','Personal and direct'],['EDUCATION','Structured and explanatory'],['PROGRAMS','Time-based and participatory'],['CONTENT','Open and discoverable'],['COMMUNITY','Collective and relational']];
const caps=['Brand Strategy','Visual Identity','Information Architecture','Web Design','UX / UI','Editorial Systems','Content Design','Responsive Design'];
const programs=[['WORKSHOP','Understanding emotional boundaries','12 October','Registration open'],['GROUP PROGRAM','Relationships in practice','05 November','Registration open'],['TALK','Care and community','Archive','Watch recording']];
const resources=[['ARTICLE','The language of boundaries','Relationships · 8 min'],['GUIDE','A practical map for difficult conversations','Download · PDF'],['VIDEO','Care as a collective practice','Community · 18 min'],['WORKSHOP','Listening without disappearing','Relationships · Online'],['ARTICLE','What support can look like','Emotional health · 6 min'],['GUIDE','Notes for everyday self-knowledge','Individual · PDF']];
---
<BaseLayout locale={locale} title="Raíces Universales — A place for care, learning and connection" description="Original identity and website design, expanded into a contemporary content and service ecosystem.">
<article class="ru">
<header class="ru-hero ru-wrap"><a href={`${root}#projects`}>← {es?'Todos los proyectos':'All projects'}</a><div class="ru-meta"><span>RAÍCES UNIVERSALES / PSYCHOLOGY · EDUCATION · COMMUNITY</span><span>ORIGINAL IDENTITY + WEBSITE</span></div><h1>Different needs.<br/><em>One coherent place.</em></h1><div class="ru-intro"><p>Raíces Universales brings psychotherapy, education, programs and community initiatives into a single platform. The design challenge was to create an identity capable of holding those different experiences together without making them feel institutional, fragmented or interchangeable.</p><p>I developed the visual identity and website as a shared system: one language connecting services, knowledge and participation. This case study also explores how that original foundation could expand today into a broader digital content and service ecosystem.</p></div></header>
<div class="ru-hero-art ru-wide"><DesignTodo note="CÉSAR: diseñar aquí hero ecosystem Raíces Universales"/><div class="ru-home"><header><img src="/projects/varios/LogoRaicesUniversales_Light-ICON.svg" alt=""/><span>Therapy &nbsp; Learn &nbsp; Programs &nbsp; Community</span></header><small>SUPPORT · KNOWLEDGE · COMMUNITY</small><h2>A place to<br/>connect, learn<br/><em>and belong.</em></h2><p>Psychotherapy, education and shared experiences in one connected space.</p><div><span>THERAPY →</span><span>LEARNING →</span><span>PROGRAMS →</span></div></div><img class="ru-social" src="/projects/raicesuniversales/RedesSociales_Enero 2022-13.jpg" alt="Original Raíces Universales social media work"/><div class="ru-mobile"><small>RAÍCES UNIVERSALES</small><h3>What brings<br/>you here?</h3>{['I need support','I want to learn','I want to participate'].map(x=><span>{x} →</span>)}</div></div>
<section class="ru-section ru-wrap"><b>01</b><div><small>01 / CONTEXT</small><h2>One identity for several ways of helping.</h2><p>Raíces Universales was not a single-service practice. Its communication needed to accommodate individual support, learning, group experiences, educational content and community participation. Each area carries a different rhythm and level of commitment.</p></div></section>
<div class="ru-ecosystem ru-wide"><DesignTodo note="CÉSAR: diseñar aquí mapa editorial del ecosistema"/><div class="ru-center">RAÍCES<br/>UNIVERSALES</div>{areas.map(([a,b],i)=><article style={`--i:${i}`}><span>0{i+1}</span><h3>{a}</h3><p>{b}</p></article>)}</div>
<section class="ru-section ru-wrap"><b>02</b><div><small>02 / BRAND STRATEGY</small><h2>Roots as structure, not decoration.</h2><p>A root system connects, supports and allows different forms of growth to emerge from the same foundation. The identity uses that idea structurally through connection, continuity, branching, rhythm and shared origin.</p></div></section>
<div class="ru-mark ru-wide"><DesignTodo note="CÉSAR: colocar aquí original identity archive y construcción del símbolo"/><div class="mark-symbol"><img src="/projects/varios/LogoRaicesUniversales_Light-ICON.svg" alt="Raíces Universales original symbol"/></div><div><small>ORIGINAL PROFESSIONAL WORK / IDENTITY</small><h2>RAÍCES<br/>UNIVERSALES</h2><p>Connection / continuity / shared origin</p><div class="mark-scale">{[1,2,3,4].map(i=><img src="/projects/varios/LogoRaicesUniversales_Light-ICON.svg" alt="" style={`width:${i*35}px`}/>)}</div></div></div>
<section class="ru-section ru-wrap"><b>03</b><div><small>03 / VISUAL SYSTEM</small><h2>Calm enough for trust.<br/><em>Structured enough for information.</em></h2><p>Deep green establishes continuity and stability. A lighter botanical tone introduces openness and differentiation. Warm paper neutrals prevent the identity from feeling clinical.</p></div></section>
<div class="ru-brand ru-wide"><div class="ru-type"><small>EDITORIAL / DIGITAL</small><strong>Aa</strong><span>Ideas need<br/>room to breathe.</span></div><div class="ru-colors"><i>#354A3C</i><i>#C8D8A0</i><i>#F1EEE6</i></div><div class="ru-hierarchy"><small>CONTENT HIERARCHY</small><h2>Understanding emotional boundaries</h2><p>A practical introduction to recognizing limits, needs and shared responsibility.</p><span>ARTICLE · 8 MIN READ · RELATIONSHIPS</span></div></div>
<section class="ru-section ru-wrap"><b>04</b><div><small>04 / INFORMATION ARCHITECTURE</small><span class="ru-chip">Contemporary exploration</span><h2>Different visitors arrive with different questions.</h2><p>A person looking for therapy does not navigate with the same intent as someone looking for a workshop, an article or a community activity.</p></div></section>
<div class="ru-ia ru-wide"><DesignTodo note="CÉSAR: diseñar aquí mapa de arquitectura de información"/>{[['I NEED SUPPORT','Therapy','Contact'],['I WANT TO LEARN','Courses · Workshops','Resources'],['I WANT TO PARTICIPATE','Programs · Events','Community'],['I WANT TO EXPLORE','Articles · Resources','About']].map(([a,b,c],i)=><article><small>0{i+1} / VISITOR INTENT</small><h3>{a}</h3><i>↓</i><b>{b}</b><span>{c} →</span></article>)}</div>
<section class="ru-section ru-wrap"><b>05</b><div><small>05 / DIGITAL EXPERIENCE</small><span class="ru-chip solid">Original professional work</span><h2>A website that gives each need a clear entrance.</h2><p>The website translates the brand into navigation, hierarchy and action. Color distinguishes content, typography establishes depth and recurring patterns make different programs recognizable as part of the same organization.</p></div></section>
<div class="ru-original-web ru-wide"><DesignTodo note="CÉSAR: mostrar aquí website original"/><img src="/placeholders/raicesuniversales-system.svg" alt="Raíces Universales original website material"/><aside><small>ORIGINAL WEBSITE / SELECTED VIEW</small><strong>Identity translated into navigation, hierarchy and action.</strong><span>DESIGNED BY CÉSAR / PROFESSIONAL WORK</span></aside></div>
<section class="ru-section ru-wrap"><b>06</b><div><small>06 / HOMEPAGE</small><h2>Start with the reason people came.</h2><p>The homepage can work as a map of needs rather than a promotional poster. The original work establishes the foundation; this contemporary structure makes those entrances more explicit.</p></div></section>
<div class="ru-homepage ru-wide"><DesignTodo note="CÉSAR: diseñar aquí contemporary homepage exploration"/><header><b>RAÍCES UNIVERSALES</b><span>Therapy &nbsp; Learning &nbsp; Programs &nbsp; About</span><i>Contact</i></header><main><small>SUPPORT · KNOWLEDGE · COMMUNITY</small><h2>Support, knowledge<br/>and community<br/><em>in one place.</em></h2><div>{['THERAPY','LEARNING','PROGRAMS'].map((x,i)=><article><span>0{i+1}</span><h3>{x}</h3><p>{['Personal support and psychotherapy.','Courses, workshops and resources.','Shared spaces and group experiences.'][i]}</p><b>Explore →</b></article>)}</div></main></div>
<section class="ru-section ru-wrap"><b>07</b><div><small>07 / SERVICES</small><h2>Sensitive information needs plain language.</h2><p>Therapy pages should answer practical questions without turning care into a sales funnel: what the service is, who provides it, how it works, available formats and how to make contact.</p></div></section>
<div class="ru-therapy ru-wide"><DesignTodo note="CÉSAR: diseñar aquí página de terapia"/><div><small>SERVICE / PSYCHOTHERAPY</small><h2>Individual psychotherapy.</h2><p>A space for listening, reflection and professional support, explained without promises or unnecessary clinical language.</p><h3>How the process begins</h3>{['Initial contact','First conversation','Ongoing sessions'].map((x,i)=><span><b>0{i+1}</b>{x}</span>)}</div><aside><small>PROFESSIONAL</small><h3>Georgina Niño</h3><p>Psychologist / Psychotherapist</p><hr/><small>FORMAT</small><p>Online / In person<br/>Subject to availability</p><button>Request information →</button></aside></div>
<section class="ru-section ru-wrap"><b>08</b><div><small>08 / PROGRAM SYSTEM</small><h2>Temporary programs need a permanent visual logic.</h2><p>Workshops, courses, talks and group activities change over time. A repeatable framework lets new initiatives appear without requiring a new identity every month.</p></div></section>
<div class="ru-programs ru-wide"><DesignTodo note="CÉSAR: diseñar aquí sistema de programas"/>{programs.map(([type,title,date,status],i)=><article><small>{type} / 0{i+1}</small><h3>{title}</h3><p>{date} · Online</p><span>{status}</span><b>View program →</b></article>)}</div>
<section class="ru-section ru-wrap"><b>09</b><div><small>09 / EDUCATION</small><h2>Educational content deserves its own rhythm.</h2><p>Articles, guides, workshops and teaching materials use a more editorial layer of the identity: stronger reading hierarchy, generous margins and clear separation between explanation and action.</p></div></section>
<article class="ru-article ru-wide"><div class="article-meta"><small>ARTICLE / RELATIONSHIPS</small><span>8 MIN READ</span><span>GEORGINA NIÑO</span></div><h1>The language<br/>of boundaries.</h1><div class="article-body"><aside>Boundaries are not walls. They describe the conditions that allow a relationship to remain understandable.</aside><p>Talking about boundaries often reduces a complex relational practice to a list of rules. A more useful approach begins with attention: what changes in us, what becomes difficult to name, and which responsibilities belong to each person.</p></div></article>
<section class="ru-section ru-wrap"><b>10</b><div><small>10 / CONTENT SYSTEM</small><span class="ru-chip">Conceptual extension</span><h2>From social posts to a reusable knowledge library.</h2><p>A structured resource library gives educational material a longer life. Resources can be organized by theme, format and audience while remaining connected to relevant services and programs.</p></div></section>
<div class="ru-library ru-wide"><DesignTodo note="CÉSAR: diseñar aquí resource library"/><header><div><small>KNOWLEDGE LIBRARY</small><h2>Explore resources.</h2></div><input placeholder="Search by topic or format"/></header><nav><span>TOPIC / All · Relationships · Emotional health · Family · Community</span><span>FORMAT / Article · Guide · Video · Workshop</span></nav><main>{resources.map(([a,b,c],i)=><article class:list={{featured:i===0}}><small>{a}</small><h3>{b}</h3><p>{c}</p><b>Open resource →</b></article>)}</main></div>
<section class="ru-section ru-wrap"><b>11</b><div><small>11 / EDITORIAL DESIGN</small><h2>A brand that can explain, not just announce.</h2><p>The system handles short announcements, long-form educational material, quotes, program details and practical information without losing visual continuity.</p></div></section>
<div class="ru-editorial ru-wide"><DesignTodo note="CÉSAR: diseñar aquí editorial content system"/><div class="guide"><small>PRACTICAL GUIDE / 01</small><h2>Conversations<br/>that need care.</h2><span>A framework for listening, limits and repair.</span></div><div class="workbook"><small>WORKSHOP WORKBOOK</small><h3>Understanding emotional boundaries</h3><b>SESSION 01—03</b></div><div class="quote"><p>“Clarity can be a form of care.”</p><small>RAÍCES / NOTES</small></div><div class="newsletter"><small>RAÍCES LETTER / 018</small><h3>Notes on support and participation</h3></div></div>
<section class="ru-section ru-wrap"><b>12</b><div><small>12 / SOCIAL SYSTEM</small><h2>Social content as part of the identity, not a parallel brand.</h2><p>The original social material demonstrates a working content system. A contemporary extension can tighten the hierarchy without erasing that professional archive.</p></div></section>
<div class="ru-social-grid ru-wide"><DesignTodo note="CÉSAR: colocar aquí social media original"/>{['01','04','08','10','13','16'].map(x=><img src={`/projects/raicesuniversales/RedesSociales_Enero 2022-${x}.jpg`} alt="Original Raíces Universales social media design" loading="lazy"/>)}</div>
<section class="ru-section ru-wrap"><b>13</b><div><small>13 / COMMUNITY</small><h2>Participation needs visibility.</h2><p>Giving initiatives their own structure allows visitors to understand how to participate rather than simply reading that a community exists.</p></div></section>
<div class="ru-community ru-wide"><div><small>CURRENT INITIATIVE</small><h2>Listening circles.</h2><p>Small group conversations around care, relationships and collective experience.</p><button>See upcoming session →</button></div><aside><span>UPCOMING EVENT <b>12 OCT / ONLINE</b></span><span>ACTIVE GROUP <b>Relationships in practice</b></span><span>OPEN RESOURCE <b>Care as a collective practice</b></span><span>NEWSLETTER <b>Receive monthly notes →</b></span></aside></div>
<section class="ru-section ru-wrap"><b>14</b><div><small>14 / SERVICE ENTRY</small><span class="ru-chip">Conceptual extension</span><h2>The first interaction should reduce uncertainty.</h2><p>A structured contact experience can route different needs without forcing everyone through the same generic form or requesting unnecessary sensitive information.</p></div></section>
<div class="ru-contact ru-wide"><DesignTodo note="CÉSAR: diseñar aquí contact routing flow"/><div><small>HOW CAN WE HELP?</small><h2>Choose the closest option.</h2>{["I'm looking for therapy","I'm interested in a program","I have a general question","I want to collaborate"].map((x,i)=><button class:list={{active:i===0}}><span>0{i+1}</span>{x}<b>→</b></button>)}</div><aside><small>NEXT STEP</small><h3>Request information about therapy.</h3><label>YOUR NAME<input/></label><label>HOW SHOULD WE CONTACT YOU?<input placeholder="Email or phone"/></label><button>Continue →</button><p>No clinical history is requested in this form.</p></aside></div>
<section class="ru-section ru-wrap"><b>15</b><div><small>15 / RESPONSIVE DESIGN</small><h2>The system needs to remain calm on a small screen.</h2><p>Long-form reading, service information, program registration and contact each require different responsive behavior.</p></div></section>
<div class="ru-phones ru-wide"><DesignTodo note="CÉSAR: producir aquí responsive sequence"/>{[['HOME','What brings you here?'],['THERAPY','Individual psychotherapy'],['PROGRAM','Understanding boundaries'],['ARTICLE','The language of boundaries'],['CONTACT','How can we help?']].map(([a,b],i)=><article><header><b>RAÍCES</b><span>0{i+1}</span></header><small>{a}</small><h3>{b}</h3><i></i><p>{i===0?'Support · Learning · Programs':'Clear information, one next step.'}</p><button>Continue →</button></article>)}</div>
<section class="ru-section ru-wrap"><b>16</b><div><small>16 / DESIGN SYSTEM</small><h2>Enough structure to grow without becoming rigid.</h2><p>Shared typography, spacing, cards, tags and navigation patterns allow new content to be introduced while preserving a recognizable voice.</p></div></section>
<div class="ru-system ru-wide"><DesignTodo note="CÉSAR: diseñar aquí editorial design system board"/><header><span>RAÍCES / CONTENT SYSTEM</span><b>LAYOUT · TYPE · TAXONOMY</b></header><div><h2>Display / 72</h2><h3>Heading / 36</h3><p>Body / 18 — Comfortable reading measure and rhythm for longer educational content.</p><aside>{['THERAPY','PROGRAM','ARTICLE','RESOURCE','COMMUNITY'].map(x=><span>{x}</span>)}</aside><button>Primary action →</button><button class="soft">Secondary action</button></div></div>
<section class="ru-section ru-wrap"><b>17</b><div><small>17 / IMAGE LANGUAGE</small><h2>Human without becoming sentimental.</h2><p>The image direction favors environments, gestures, material detail and moments of interaction over exaggerated emotional stock photography. The goal is presence rather than performance.</p></div></section>
<div class="ru-photo-direction ru-wide"><DesignTodo note="CÉSAR: producir aquí moodboard documental de fotografía"/><div><small>01 / NATURAL LIGHT</small></div><div><small>02 / REAL ENVIRONMENTS</small></div><div><small>03 / GESTURES + MATERIALS</small></div><div><small>04 / SMALL GROUPS</small></div><aside>Natural light<br/>Open space<br/>Environmental portraiture<br/>Botanical detail, selectively</aside></div>
<section class="ru-section ru-wrap"><b>18</b><div><small>18 / BRAND APPLICATION</small><h2>The same tone beyond the website.</h2><p>Educational guides, program materials, stationery and event communication use the same hierarchy and palette without depending on digital interface patterns.</p></div></section>
<div class="ru-print ru-wide"><div class="poster"><small>WORKSHOP / OCT 12</small><h2>Understanding<br/>emotional<br/>boundaries.</h2></div><div class="folder">RAÍCES<br/>UNIVERSALES</div><div class="book"><small>PRACTICAL GUIDE</small><h3>Notes for difficult conversations</h3></div></div>
<section class="ru-original"><div class="ru-wrap original-copy"><div><small>19 / ORIGINAL WORK</small><span class="ru-chip solid">Original professional work</span><h2>The system as originally delivered.</h2></div><p>The visual identity and website shown here were developed as professional work for Raíces Universales. This archive preserves the original project context before the contemporary extensions presented elsewhere.</p></div><div class="ru-original-grid ru-wide"><img src="/projects/raicesuniversales/RedesSociales_Enero-2022.jpg" alt="Original Raíces Universales professional work"/><img src="/projects/raicesuniversales/RedesSociales_Enero 2022-05.jpg" alt="Original social design"/><img src="/projects/raicesuniversales/RedesSociales_Enero 2022-12.jpg" alt="Original social design"/><div><DesignTodo note="CÉSAR: colocar aquí original identity archive"/><img src="/placeholders/raicesuniversales-cover.svg" alt="Raíces Universales identity archive placeholder"/></div></div></section>
<section class="ru-section ru-wrap"><b>20</b><div><small>20 / CONTEMPORARY EXTENSION</small><span class="ru-chip">2026 conceptual extension</span><h2>What the system can become.</h2><p>The conceptual extensions explore how the same brand can support a growing ecosystem of services, programs, knowledge and participation without rewriting the history of the original commission.</p></div></section>
<div class="ru-contemporary ru-wide"><DesignTodo note="CÉSAR: diseñar aquí contemporary ecosystem"/><small>2026 / CONCEPTUAL EXTENSION</small><h2>CARE<br/><em>KNOWLEDGE</em><br/>PARTICIPATION</h2><div>{['RESOURCE LIBRARY','PROGRAM SYSTEM','CONTACT ROUTING','RESPONSIVE EDITORIAL'].map(x=><span>{x} →</span>)}</div></div>
<section class="ru-reflection ru-wrap"><b>21</b><div><small>21 / REFLECTION</small><h2>A sensitive brand still needs strong architecture.</h2><p>Warmth and structure are not competing goals. The identity creates emotional continuity. Information architecture creates orientation. Editorial hierarchy creates understanding. Together, they allow one organization to speak about care, education and community without flattening them into the same experience.</p><div>{caps.map(x=><span>{x}</span>)}</div><small>Original identity and website design + contemporary conceptual extension.</small></div></section>
<div class="ru-final ru-wide"><DesignTodo note="CÉSAR: diseñar aquí final ecosystem image"/><small>ONE IDENTITY / MANY WAYS TO CONNECT</small><h2>CARE.<br/>LEARNING.<br/><em>COMMUNITY.</em></h2></div>
<a class="ru-next ru-wrap" href={`${root}project/steps/`}><span>NEXT PROJECT</span><strong>Steps</strong><b>↗</b></a>
</article>
</BaseLayout>

